		title: "Three-step form",
		description: "Details, confirm, success — one `defineSheetMachine`, one `BottomSheet.Steps`. NEXT stays disabled until the guard passes, and the sheet's height glides to each step rather than jumping: the step measures, the dynamic snap point moves, and the panel follows with the same spring the body is using. The confirm step is `dismissible: false`, so a swipe down and a tap on the scrim do nothing there; the success step names `snapPoints: [\"35%\"]` and is sized by them. Closing resets the machine, so the next open starts at details.",
